Aisha (CS): Hey team — customer (FinTrack) reports repeated tool/function call failures after yesterday's model rollout. They see schema validation errors like `missing required property \"amount\"` even though their tool schema marks `amount` as optional. Repro steps below. Can @Jae (eng-ml) / @Tom (eng-platform) take a look? :eyes:

Aisha (CS): Repro steps we ran (minimal):
1) POST /v1/chat with model=redwood-prod-2026-03
2) system prompt includes our paid-invoice fewshot examples (attached)
3) user asks `charge customer for invoice 1234`
4) model returns a function call but validation fails on server with 422

Aisha (CS): Example request payload:
```json
{
  \"model\": \"redwood-prod-2026-03\",
  \"messages\": [
    {\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"<FEWSHOT_EXAMPLES>\"},
    {\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Charge customer 1234 for $56.78\"}
  ],
  \"functions\": [{\"name\":\"charge_card\",\"parameters\": {\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"invoice_id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"amount\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[]}}]
}
```

Aisha (CS): Server log snippet: `Function call parsed -> arguments: {\\\"invoice_id\\\": \\\"1234\\\"} -> validate() -> error: missing required property \\\"amount\\\"` (schema library says amount optional but validator treats it as required)

Jae (eng-ml): Oof. Can you paste the raw model output (function call payload) that the model returned? Need to see if the model is emitting a different arg shape or including stray text from examples.

Aisha (CS): Pasted model output below (raw):
```json
{
  \"role\": \"assistant\",
  \"content\": null,
  \"function_call\": {
    \"name\": \"charge_card\",
    \"arguments\": "{\n      \\\"invoice\\\": \\\"1234\\\",\n      \\\"amount\\\": null,\n      \\\"notes\\\": \\\"SEE BELOW: apply-discount 10%\\\"\n    }"
  }
}
```

Aisha (CS): Note: `amount` is present but null, and model added a bunch of freeform `notes` text that looks like it was copied from one of the few-shot examples in the system prompt. Customer says their example in docs uses `notes` for human text but never includes `amount:null`.

Tom (eng-platform): Two quick possibilities: (1) few-shot examples in the system prompt include `amount: null` or a line like `NOTE: pending` which could bias the model into emitting nulls, (2) our prompt sanitizer/templating step might be munging the function schema into examples incorrectly. I just checked the deploy history — we rolled redwood-prod-2026-03 at 1965370000 with a small prompt templating change.

infra-bot: Deploy 1965370000 -> redwood-prod-2026-03 completed by @release-bot at 2026-03-16T02:14:00Z. Canary 100%

Jae (eng-ml): The model sometimes generalizes from few-shot examples into the generated JSON. If any example shows `amount` as `null` or includes inline human commentary like `// apply discount`, the decoder can emit that text inside `arguments` as a string or null. Two mitigations: (A) remove or sanitize problematic few-shot examples in the system prompt ASAP, (B) patch the function-args postprocessor to coerce/validate types before handing to schema validator.

Lena (devex): For a hotfix we can add a lightweight post-parse sanitizer on the function_call path that: trim whitespace, run JSON.parse on the `arguments` string, coerce `null` -> omit field, and reject if non-JSON tokens exist. Minimal patch suggestion (server side):
```js
// pseudo
try {
  const args = JSON.parse(function_call.arguments);
  if (args.amount === null) delete args.amount;
  // additional cleanup
  proceedWith(args);
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: send to human-review queue + log
}
```

Tom (eng-platform): Agree. I'll open an emergency patch PR to do that and add an integration test. Also adding stricter logging to capture which system prompt snippet influenced the completion so we can correlate.

Jae (eng-ml): Longer term we should: (1) discourage freeform few-shot examples that include inline developer notes, (2) convert few-shot examples into structured assistant messages or use `tool`-only examples (explicit function_call objects), (3) add an eval that checks for argument typing and stray commentary in `arguments` strings.

Aisha (CS): Customer is blocked in prod — requesting ETA for hotfix and whether we can rollback model to previous version. They prefer rollback if patch takes >30m.

Tom (eng-platform): I can rollback the traffic to redwood-prod-2026-02 (previous) in ~10m if needed. Patch PR for sanitizer in ~15-30m, deploy in ~45m if CI green. Which do you want?

Aisha (CS): Please rollback first. We'll communicate to customer and then request a follow-up once sanitizer is live.

Jae (eng-ml): FYI if you rollback, still recommend scanning the system prompt sets for other customers. I'll run a quick grep across our canned few-shot templates for `null` and `NOTE:` and report back here.

Lena (devex): I'll add a short doc blurb for Support about best practices: \"avoid inline dev comments in few-shot examples; prefer explicit `function_call` examples\". Will ping #docs once ready. :memo:

Aisha (CS): Thanks all. I've informed FinTrack we're rolling back now and will follow up when sanitizer is deployed. Assigning follow-up owners: @Tom (rollback + patch), @Jae (prompt scan + eval), @Lena (support doc).

Tom (eng-platform): Rolling back to redwood-prod-2026-02 now. infra-bot will post when done.

infra-bot: Rollback complete -> redwood-prod-2026-02 now serving 100% (performed by @release-bot).

Jae (eng-ml): Quick status: grep found 3 few-shot templates with `NOTE:` style comments and 1 template that uses `amount: null` example. I'll open PRs to sanitize those patterns. ETA ~2h for cleanup + tests.

Aisha (CS): Great. Customer updated: service back to previous model, they're testing. They've asked for postmortem and corrective actions — I'll draft and share. :white_check_mark:

Lena (devex): Filed a short CS playbook entry and will link the PRs once they exist.

Aisha (CS): Closing the loop here — will re-open if FinTrack reports any residual issues. Thanks team! :pray:
